# wpus — checkout attributes
#
# A public repository is cloned onto Linux, macOS, and Windows (mostly WSL,
# but native tooling happens too). These rules make a checkout byte-identical
# everywhere, which matters for a security tool: a diff caused by a stray CR
# would otherwise show up as a "changed" core file in someone's audit.

# Normalize to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit, because these are the files where a CRLF would actually break
# something (shebangs, CI, and the shell installer).
*.go        text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.mod       text eol=lf
*.sum       text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf
LICENSE     text eol=lf
.gitignore  text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Binary fixtures and archives: never touch their bytes.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.tgz  binary

# GitHub language statistics: prose is not source code.
docs/**            linguist-documentation
CHANGELOG.md       linguist-documentation
CONTRIBUTING.md    linguist-documentation
SECURITY.md        linguist-documentation
LICENSE            linguist-documentation
testdata/**        linguist-documentation
